{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p5-a6ea57bd","text":"Need decide exact UI and persistence. We need maybe add volume/mute in Display menu instead of new Audio to keep main menu 8. User asks menu volume and mute; adding Audio is fine. Main max 9, 9 items fits; but `Menu.MaxItems=9`, window draws 9 entries, main 9 exactly. Good. If we add Audio after Display, no issue. But adding new main item could shift numeric indices used in ProcessCommand for joy and fps? `menuList[1]`, `menuList[2]` within submenus unaffected. Fine.

Alternative put Audio items in Display menu; no new submenu, easier. But volume/mute are audio not display. New Audio menu cleaner.

Potential issue: Menu starts at selectedItem 0; after volume changes, `menuList[1]` text update. Fine.

### Persist strategy
`AppSettings.Save` at each change or rely on Cleanup. Existing `ShowSpeed` changes in Renderer but only saves at cleanup. For volume, user could expect setting saved immediately; do both? Calling Save on each change is simple and ensures. It's okay. But writing from menu while settings file may be locked by another instance? catches. Fine.
