- **VSync on:** unchanged; `Present()` still runs each loop and blocks on the display refresh.
- **VSync off:** presentation is paced to `C64Machine.FrameDurationTicks` — the same 19.95 ms / 50.125 fps interval used by the emulation thread — instead of submitting frames at roughly 100 Hz.
- The loop polls SDL events during the wait in short 1–5 ms sleeps, so input remains responsive.
- If a present overruns its deadline, the cadence restarts from the next slot rather than presenting a burst of catch-up frames.
- Fast-forward uses a half-length interval so accelerated emulation remains visibly faster.

The shared frame duration is exposed at [C64Machine.cs:29](C64Emulator/C64Machine.cs#L29), and [README.md:58](README.md#L58) documents the behavior.

